    = note: What `add` takes is hashed by its own hash, so it has to have one: an integer, a `String`, a `bool`, a `scalar`, `Bytes`, a tuple, list or option of those, or a type of yours that hashes. A float doesn't (`NaN` isn't equal to itself).
    = help: Feed it the parts `eq` compares that hash, such as an integer or a text made from the value.
